48:["$","details","Is partnership registration mandatory?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-4","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Is partnership registration mandatory?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"No. The Indian Partnership Act, 1932, does not compel registration, and a firm can legally operate without it. However, section 69 prevents an unregistered firm or its partners from suing to enforce a contractual right against the firm or against a third party. In practice that means an unregistered firm cannot go to court to recover money a customer owes it, so we recommend registering."}]}]]}]
49:["$","details","What documents are needed?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-5","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What documents are needed?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"PAN, Aadhaar, identity proof, address proof and a photograph for each partner, the partnership deed executed on stamp paper, proof of the firm's place of business, a rent agreement if the premises are rented, and a no-objection certificate from the owner."}]}]]}]
4a:["$","details","What is the registration process?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-6","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What is the registration process?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The partners agree their terms, a deed is drafted and executed on stamp paper of the value prescribed by the state, the firm applies for its own PAN, and an application is filed with the Registrar of Firms for the state with the deed and supporting proofs. The Registrar issues a certificate of registration on approval."}]}]]}]
4b:["$","details","How is a partnership firm different from an LLP?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-7","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is a partnership firm different from an LLP?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The difference that matters most is liability. In a partnership firm the partners are personally liable without limit, including for the acts of the other partners. In an LLP, liability is limited to the agreed contribution and a partner is not personally liable for another partner's wrongful acts. An LLP is also a separate legal entity and can hold property in its own name, but it carries annual ROC filing obligations that a partnership firm does not."}]}]]}]
4c:["$","details","Can a partnership firm be converted into an LLP or a company later?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-8","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can a partnership firm be converted into an LLP or a company later?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. The LLP Act and the Companies Act both provide routes for converting a registered partnership firm into an LLP or into a company, subject to conditions including the consent of all partners. Many firms start as a partnership and convert once the business grows or once limited liability becomes a real concern."}]}]]}]
4d:["$","details","How is a partnership firm taxed?",{"className":"group","id":"partnership-registration-faq-9","name":"partnership-registration-faq","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-5 text-left font-semibold text-secondary marker:hidden hover:bg-muted/60 sm:px-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"How is a partnership firm taxed?"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-primary transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-5 pb-6 text-muted-foreground sm:px-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"The firm is assessed to income tax as a separate entity at the rate applicable to firms, plus applicable surcharge and cess. A partner's share of the firm's profit is exempt in the partner's own hands because it has already been taxed in the firm, but interest on capital and remuneration received from the firm are taxable for the partner, and are deductible for the firm only within the limits set by section 40(b)."}]}]]}]
